WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.794
JIM: (whistles) North!

00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:05.213
-Yeah!
-HUDSON: Yeah!

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.132
-JIM: We're goin' in the canoe!
-TORI: Come on, in the boat,
please.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.425
Good boy!

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:11.511
Okay, hon, ready?

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.890
JIM: We're heading back to camp
with the wood we foraged.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.100
HUDSON: Yeah!

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.601
JIM (off screen):
All right, perfect!

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.770
We made it through
the first night no problem,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.732
but now, we wanna make the site
a little more comfortable,

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:26.109
so we'll use the wood
to build some furniture,

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:29.988
so we can make it
as much like home
for the kids as we can.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:33.867
We'll have to build
a lotta things like this
when we live off-grid,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:36.453
so it'll be good
practice for all of us.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:38.663
Look, honey, we're home!

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.957
TORI: This is so relaxing,
actually, eh?

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:42.167
-JIM: Oh, I love it.
-TORI: To have this all

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.835
-set up, and--
-JIM: I know.

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:46.046
TORI (off screen):
Look at Wes sitting up,
though, eh?

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.756
-Sitting all the way
up on his own.
-JIM (off screen): Wow!

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:49.007
-He's doin' so well.
-TORI: Not even leaning.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:49.966
JIM: Good job, Wes!

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.552
TORI:
Yeah, we're talkin' about you!

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.179
JIM (off screen):
You're doin' so good!

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:58.183
Since Wesley has been
diagnosed with FOXG1 syndrome,

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:01.061
it's been reiterated
to us with pediatricians,

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.353
with other specialists,

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:04.731
that bringing Wesley
out into nature,

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.608
exposing him to some elements,

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.693
the better it will be
for his development.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:12.947
Wesley's core muscles
have really strengthened up
a lot, eh, Tori?

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.449
-TORI (off screen):
Yeah, big time.
-JIM (off screen): Yeah, just

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:16.201
from him sittin'
in the canoe, I bet,

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.869
-and just havin'
to keep stable there.
-TORI: Look at him.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:18.828
Yay!

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:19.954
JIM:
I'm gonna be makin' furniture.

00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:21.831
Should I make
a table or chairs first?

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.875
-TORI: Definitely a chair.
-JIM: Chair?

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:25.126
But what are you gonna sit on?

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.419
Just kidding.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:33.468
Right now,
I am building a couple chairs.

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:37.263
I'm just taking
four pieces of wood
and making two triangles.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.641
One of these triangles
is gonna be a seat,

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:41.851
and the other triangle
is gonna be a backrest.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:45.647
I've always thought
it was interesting

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:47.107
to try to make
stuff for yourself,

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.525
ever since I was a little kid.

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:51.402
It's always fun
to see what you can

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:53.863
kinda make with your hands
with the materials around you,

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:56.282
as opposed to always relying
on store-bought items.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.368
TORI: Before we left home,

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.788
Jim and I made a high-calorie
trail food called pemmican.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.832
It's made
from dehydrated berries,

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:05.959
bison meat,
and rendered animal fat.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.170
I'm adding it to a stew
with some veggies.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.798
It's the perfect
high-nutrition meal

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:14.884
after a long day
of hiking and foraging.

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:17.804
JIM:
This is all just kind of
practice, if you will, for, um,

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:21.516
when we are gonna spend much
more time at an off-grid cabin

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:24.144
that hopefully we can build,
maybe in the near future.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.648
Yeah, like that.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.191
Like that.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:39.367
Tori... Ready for a chair?

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.661
But crafted by the hand
of the Man of the Wilder,

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.246
-Jim Baird himself.
-TORI: Whoa!

00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:45.707
-JIM:
That's nice enough for that...
-TORI: Plop it right there.

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:47.458
JIM:
...champion booty
of yours or what?

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:48.793
Huh?

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.628
TORI: Should I test it out?

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:53.882
-JIM: Yeah, there you go.
-TORI: I'm scared.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.258
-JIM: No, it's good!
-TORI: Oh!

00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:57.010
JIM:
Yeah, it's, kind of,
a lean-backy feel.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.720
-TORI: Oh, I--
-JIM: Do you like it?

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.305
TORI: Yeah, I like this.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:02.432
JIM: Look at mine, hon, huh?

00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:04.767
-TORI: Look at you.
-JIM: Right?

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:08.146
(groans)
Oh, this one is great, too.

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:10.565
That is comfy. Look at that.

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:12.984
-That's chill.
Good job, honey.
-TORI: Good job!

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:14.861
-JIM: Good day.
-TORI: Crushed it.

